## Performance Considerations

### Memory

- Chart geometry memoized, only recalculates on data/dimension change
- SharedValues don't trigger React re-renders
- Context value stable across renders

### CPU

- Gesture handlers run on UI thread via worklets
- Path calculations done once in JavaScript, then cached
- D3 scales and curves computed efficiently

### Best Practices

- Keep `data` memoized if computed from props
- Avoid re-creating callback functions on every render
- Use `React.memo` on parent components if passing many props
- Paginate or downsample data for 10k+ points

## Troubleshooting

### Chart not responding to touch

- Ensure `isInteractive` is enabled (default: `true`)
- Verify long-press duration (250ms required)
- Ensure no parent gesture handlers blocking

### Animation not working on exit

- Verify `isFocusMode` updates before `cursorData`
- Check `EtAnimatedCount` has `animate={!isFocusMode}`
- Ensure `requestAnimationFrame` delay for `onCursorDataChange(null)`

### Values not updating

- Verify `onCursorDataChange` callback is provided
- Check `data` is not empty
- Ensure `selectedValue` is a valid SharedValue

### Performance issues

- Reduce dataset size (downsample to ~100-500 points)
- Check for excessive parent re-renders
- Verify chart dimensions are reasonable (< 1000px)

## Migration from Redux Version

### Before (Redux)

```tsx
const cursorData = useSelector(selectCursorData);
const isFocusMode = useSelector(selectFocusMode);

<EtLineChart data={data} selectedValue={selectedValue} />;
```

### After (Callbacks)

```tsx
const [cursorData, setCursorData] = useState(null);
const [isFocusMode, setIsFocusMode] = useState(false);

<EtLineChart data={data} selectedValue={selectedValue} onFocusModeChange={setIsFocusMode} onCursorDataChange={setCursorData} />;
```

## Design System Integration

The chart consumes V2 color tokens from `useEtoroTheme()`. Each visual slot maps to a token as follows:

| Slot | V2 token |
| --- | --- |
| Line color (positive / negative) | `verdictPositive600` / `verdictNegative600` |
| Cursor stroke (default) | `verdictPositive600` |
| Fade-mask gradient (start / end) | `verdictPositive600Opacity50` (low-alpha) / `verdictPositive600` (solid) — both serve as alpha values for the Skia `Mask`, not visible hues |
| Area gradient under line (positive / negative) | `verdictPositive600` / `verdictNegative600` (faded via Path `opacity` prop, default 0.3) |
| Marker dots (default) | `carbon400` |
| Baseline dashed line | `carbonPrimaryDivider` |
| Cursor overlay rect | `carbon050` |
| Y-axis label chip background | `carbonSecondaryDivider` |
| Y-axis label text | `carbon900` |

Override props (`lineColor`, `cursorColor`, `markerColor`, `maskGradientColors`, `gradientColors`) bypass the defaults above, so consumers can still pin a specific color when needed.

### Behavior deltas vs. pre-V2

- **Y-axis label text** flips from light grey (`textTertiaryNeutral`) to near-black (`carbon900`) per Figma — most visible change.
- **Y-axis chip background** changes from translucent white (`bgTransparentPrimaryBright`, `#FFFFFF25`) to translucent grey (`carbonSecondaryDivider`, `#B2B2B226`). Figma's variable label `var(--primary-divider)` resolves to `#B2B2B226`, which corresponds to our `carbonSecondaryDivider` (the naming in Figma is misleading — picked by hex equivalence).
- **Light-mode area gradient under the line** shifts from bright pale `#6DFF8A` / `#FF6B6E` to saturated `verdictPositive600` / `verdictNegative600`. The hardcoded `useColorScheme` branch was removed because V2 tokens are theme-aware.
- **Marker dots in dark mode** lighten from `#4D4D4D` (`textDisabledPrimaryNeutral` dark) to `#999999` (`carbon400` dark). Light mode is unchanged (`#CCCCCC`).

